1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,720
Gloss Model reads what the docs say as contracts.

2
00:00:04,380 --> 00:00:08,140
For every declaration, the Interface builds a Contract.

3
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:12,680
It holds the signature as written, and the doc comment read as a promise.

4
00:00:13,020 --> 00:00:13,820
The summary.

5
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:16,680
Each parameter with its type and its entry.

6
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:20,240
What it returns, what it throws, and any callouts.

7
00:00:20,990 --> 00:00:24,310
It also lists the type names the declaration mentions.

8
00:00:24,670 --> 00:00:27,110
Those mentions are what the next piece uses.

9
00:00:29,133 --> 00:00:31,393
From those mentions, the Graph is drawn.

10
00:00:31,753 --> 00:00:33,673
A node is a type with its members.

11
00:00:34,133 --> 00:00:39,113
An edge says that one type mentions another, and its roles say where.

12
00:00:39,783 --> 00:00:43,523
A type can appear in a property, in a parameter, in a return,

13
00:00:43,803 --> 00:00:45,803
in a throws clause, or in a conformance.

14
00:00:46,003 --> 00:00:50,283
An edge made only of body mentions is implementation, not interface.

15
00:00:51,033 --> 00:00:52,953
And a Reason says why.

16
00:00:53,373 --> 00:00:58,133
It reads what the declaration wrote about the type it uses, in the entry for the

17
00:00:58,133 --> 00:01:01,973
parameter or in the summary, so the answer is the author's own.

18
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,120
An Interface Diff compares two interfaces.

19
00:01:07,850 --> 00:01:10,510
Things are matched by name, never by place.

20
00:01:10,790 --> 00:01:15,070
Code that only moves inside a file, or between files, is no change.

21
00:01:15,820 --> 00:01:18,280
Every difference is one of five kinds.

22
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:19,280
Added.

23
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:20,220
Removed.

24
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:23,180
Changed, when the signature or the doc differs.

25
00:01:23,880 --> 00:01:28,920
Implementation, when only what the body does differs, which changes no one's view of the interface.

26
00:01:29,660 --> 00:01:33,240
And moved, when a type keeps its name and goes to another module.

27
00:01:33,990 --> 00:01:37,610
A renamed type reads as one removed and one added.

28
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:41,320
A diff says what changed.

29
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:46,460
Change Commits says who changed it, by reading git blame, so each change can quote the

30
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:48,240
commit messages that wrote its lines.

31
00:01:48,990 --> 00:01:53,030
A Change Story says why, in the author's words.

32
00:01:53,370 --> 00:01:56,830
It lives in the repository, in a file named for the branch.

33
00:01:57,090 --> 00:02:02,170
A heading, a summary, and themes, with links to the types and members each theme is

34
00:02:02,170 --> 00:02:02,390
about.

35
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:06,440
Story Coverage then checks the story against the diff.

36
00:02:06,780 --> 00:02:09,520
Every type whose interface changed needs a theme.

37
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:11,960
Every change needs a note of its own.

38
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:14,400
And every link has to name something real.

39
00:02:15,150 --> 00:02:18,590
So the reason for a change is written down, and checked.
